The port has been mostly a one-man part-time job, at least on the coding
side. This has changed as a mac team has now been formed. (Izchak still
haven't seen your posting :-))
I'm just glad there aren't that many serious errors in the code.
There are a couple in there. For instance, with pl6, if the 
rumors and/or oracles files aren't in the directory where
Nethack is currently looking (most likely the System Folder),
it will NEVER find it. Depending on which compiler you used to
build Nethack (Lightspeed C 3 is bad, Think C 4 is a little better),
with the original 700K mem. allocation, you will run out of memory.
I've had reports that Nethack trashes memory in other heaps. I
haven't been able to reproduce this, but then I don't play that often
or for that long or run with many programs in memory.

When I was first enlisted to port Nethack, my job was to ensure that
Nethack would be available to as wide an audience as possible.
What can be hard to remember when all around you are mostly Mac II's
(or more powerful Macs) with gobs of memory is that only 14% of the Mac
population actually has a machine with more than 1 MB of memory
(from a Dataquest study done in Feb, probably has changed but how
much? - I know I was a member of the 86% in Feb.) 
A different version could be built for those with more than 1MB
with some added features.

Unfortunately, I haven't been spending lots of time on the port.
I do have other projects/hobbies. Plus sometimes at the end of the
day, after staring at a screen for umpteen hours, the last thing
I want to do is boot up my Mac and burn out my eyes some more. :-)

Also, in a previous posting, I metioned that it would be OK to
build the special level compiler and create the files and bring
them over to the Mac. A guy from the MSDOS Nethack team has
reminded me that byte-ordering would probably screw that up, i.e.
building on an Intel which has low-hi byte ordering and bring
the files over to the Mac which has hi-low byte ordering will do
you no good. The special level compiler CAN be built in pl6 on a Mac.
E-mail me with the problems and the exact procedure you're going
thru to see where the instructions need more clarification.

